Bugfix: Token requests of OAuth2 clients no longer count as failed logins

At the token endpoint of the oauth2 app, HTTP Basic carries the client id and
secret, not user credentials. When a desktop client also sent its session
cookie, as version 6.0.3 does, the request was checked like a user login with
the client id as user name: every token refresh logged "Login failed", counted
towards the brute-force protection - which then also slowed down real logins
from the same address - and ended the session. Basic credentials on
POST /apps/oauth2/api/v1/token are no longer evaluated as a user login. Nothing
changes on any other route.
